.TH BIGFLOATCMPABS 3 "2026-09-25" "BigNums 3" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigFloatCmpAbs \- compare float magnitudes exactly
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <bignums.h>

int bigFloatCmpAbs(const BigFloat *a, const BigFloat *b);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compares absolute values using exponent, bit length and aligned bits without
allocating or truncating. Zero is smaller than every nonzero magnitude.
Equivalent values with different mantissa widths compare equal. Inputs require
canonical integer mantissas; the highest limb need not have bit 31 set.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns -1, 0 or +1 as a comparison value, not an error status.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
